{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["Empty-headed ones will interpret the verse that is in the book of Ezekiel, namely 'any carcass or torn thing, of bird or of beast, the priests shall not eat,' as referring to whatever birds or beasts have torn or killed. This is nonsense, for in the Torah it is written: <b>any carcass or torn thing he shall not eat</b>. And the reason is that if he eats, he may not minister."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:40.656156109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}